{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRy3s1pvm1FVUgBNggnU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the generator so the watch should show the heart rate ranges we planned. This isn't checked on the watch yet: per your rules I didn't push to Intervals or sync. Locally, `gen.py` now writes the new format for all 4 heart rate steps.\n\n**The cause:** in `gen.py` (`hr_target`), the bottom of each range was sent as `value`. Intervals sends `{value, end}` to the watch as a zone target, and the watch snaps it to its own zones. That's exactly what `watch-notes.md` shows: each planned range came out as one of the watch's zone bands.\n\n**The fix:** the bottom is now sent as `start`, so the target is `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. Intervals sends that as a plain bpm range. It still converts percentages to bpm from its own LTHR (172), and the plan format is unchanged.\n\n**To check it:**\n1. Run `./push.sh`.\n2. Read the event back with `GET /events/{id}`. `start` should still be there and `steps` should not be empty.\n3. Sync the watch. The Float step should show 129–141, not 137–151.\n\nDelete or replace the old event 184233 first, or you'll have two copies.\n\n**From your colleague's note** (details in `ANSWER.md`):\n- **Used:** the main finding, `start` instead of `value`. It matches our case exactly, down to the same LTHR values (172 vs 168).\n- **Used as confirmation:** their failed attempts with `bpm` and `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` match ours, so I didn't retry them and kept percentages.\n- **Used:** their way of checking the result on the watch.\n- **Skipped:** the advice to add a top-level `description` in Intervals' text format. It fixes a different problem (steps not showing in the Intervals web page), which we don't have. If its text doesn't parse, Intervals wipes the steps entirely."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"inpu