he watch snaps it to its own zones. That's exactly what `watch-notes.md` shows: each planned range came out as one of the watch's zone bands.\n\n**The fix:** the bottom is now sent as `start`, so the target is `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. Intervals sends that as a plain bpm range. It still converts percentages to bpm from its own LTHR (172), and the plan format is unchanged.\n\n**To check it:**\n1. Run `./push.sh`.\n2. Read the event back with `GET /events/{id}`. `start` should still be there and `steps` should not be empty.\n3. Sync the watch. The Float step should show 129–141, not 137–151.\n\nDelete or replace the old event 184233 first, or you'll have two copies.\n\n**From your colleague's note** (details in `ANSWER.md`):\n- **Used:** the main finding, `start` instead of `value`. It matches our case exactly, down to the same LTHR values (172 vs 168).\n- **Used as confirmation:** their failed attempts with `bpm` and `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` match ours, so I didn't retry them and kept percentages.\n- **Used:** their way of checking the result on the watch.\n- **Skipped:** the advice to add a top-level `description` in Intervals' text format. It fixes a different problem (steps not showing in the Intervals web page), which we don't have. If its text doesn't parse, Intervals wipes the steps entirely.","ttft_ms":1923,"type":"result","duration_ms":28132,"uuid":"5910b38d-415e-4bab-a57f-475757628ecc","ttft_stream_ms":863,"time_to_request_ms":30,"first_content_frame_ms":864,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":2759,"cacheReadInputTokens":112458,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9569,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1542636,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":149,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
